<title>NETHERLANDS: Vendex buys shoe chain Scapino.</title>
<headline>Vendex buys shoe chain Scapino.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch retail and business services group Vendex International NV said on Friday it had acquired Scapino, a shoe and sportswear chain with branches in the Netherlands, Belgium and Germany.  </p>
<p>Vendex said it expected the acquisition to have a positive impact on its profits per share in the book year 1997/98.</p>
<p>No financial details were disclosed but it said Scapino had a net turnover of around 340 million guilders from 160 shops with 3,000 employees.</p>
<p>Most of Scapino's shops were in the Nertherlands with 14 in Belgium and a handful in Germany.</p>
<p>Vendex said it anticipated a strong increase in the number of outlets this year.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 320 504 5000</p>
</text>
